/F1 11 Tf
50 792 Td
(Live Tracking Flow) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Socket connection) Tj
T*
(The mobile app connects to the backend socket and sends a JWT in the handshake.) Tj
T*
(Backend auth middleware verifies the token and populates socket.data with userId, driverId,) Tj
T*
(and role.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Start tracking) Tj
T*
(Mobile emits driver:session:start.) Tj
T*
(Backend calls startSession\(driverId, routeId\) and creates a DriverSession row.) Tj
T*
(Backend replies with driver:session:started and a new sessionId.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Emit GPS updates) Tj
T*
(After session start the phone must start a GPS watcher or interval.) Tj
T*
(Every 1 to 5 seconds the app emits driver:location:update with the current sessionId and GPS) Tj
T*
(point.) Tj
T*
(Backend validates the payload, checks the session is still active, and writes the point.) Tj
T*
(A successful update creates a DriverLocation row and updates Driver.currentLat/currentLng.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Stop tracking) Tj
T*
(When tracking stops the client must clear the GPS watcher first and then emit) Tj
T*
(driver:session:end.) Tj
T*
(Backend marks the session ended and clears the driver throttle state.) Tj
T*
(After that, any old location update with the same sessionId is rejected as Session already) Tj
T*
(ended.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Disconnect handling) Tj
T*
(If the socket disconnects unexpectedly, the backend auto-closes any still-open sessions to) Tj
T*
(keep the DB clean.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
