(Rerouting Flow) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(rerouteActiveRoutesOnce\(\) checks active routes with driver locations.) Tj
T*
(For each active route it reads the latest DriverLocation, rebuilds the remaining nodes, and) Tj
T*
(re-runs OR-Tools from the driver current position.) Tj
T*
(If the new plan improves the remaining route by at least the configured threshold, it) Tj
T*
(updates the route and stop sequence.) Tj
T*
(If the gain is too small, it skips rerouting to avoid unnecessary disruption.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Important env values) Tj
T*
(- MAPBOX_TOKEN: required for live matrix calls.) Tj
T*
(- ORTOOLS_SERVICE_URL: URL of the Python solver service.) Tj
T*
(- PLANNER_DEPOT_LAT / PLANNER_DEPOT_LNG: optional depot override.) Tj
T*
(- PLANNER_SOLVER_TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS: OR-Tools solve timeout.) Tj
T*
(- PLANNER_REROUTE_MIN_GAIN_SECONDS: reroute threshold.) Tj
T*
(- LOCATION_MIN_INTERVAL_MS: live tracking throttle, currently 0 for demo.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Good code review explanation) Tj
T*
(The planner is an orchestration layer: it converts orders into pickup and delivery nodes,) Tj
T*
(uses Mapbox for real road travel times, sends the matrix to OR-Tools for optimization, then) Tj
T*
(persists the result and emits realtime events. Rerouting reuses the same solver starting) Tj
T*
(from the driver current position and only applies changes when the improvement is) Tj
T*
(meaningful.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Good live tracking explanation) Tj
T*
(The mobile app owns the GPS watcher. The backend only stores and validates the points it) Tj
T*
(receives. Tracking works only when the app starts the watcher after driver:session:started) Tj
T*
(and stops it before driver:session:end.) Tj
ET
